  "title": "Provider-neutral sandbox seam with a Docker adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a provider-neutral `Sandbox` trait (create / run / destroy / capabilities) plus its value types, an in-memory `FakeSandbox` double that records every call, and a Docker adapter that implements the trait by shelling out to `docker` one invocation per operation. Every argv and every response is built and read by a pure function, so the adapter is testable without a daemon; the real runner is exercised against a fake `docker` script, and a neutrality test asserts the seam's own source names no provider.",
